<title>FRANCE: Lafarge seeks to halt 97 div reinvestment.</title>
<headline>Lafarge seeks to halt 97 div reinvestment.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French building materials group Lafarge plans to suspend, for 1997, an option for shareholders to revinvest their dividends in shares, in an attempt to limit profit dilution, a Lafarge spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The board will propose at the annual general meeting that the dividend share reinvestment option not be renewed for 1997,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Chairman Bertrand Collomb revealed the plan to analysts at a briefing on Wednesday after publication of the group's results.</p>
</text>
